    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf a user triggers a `imap`, and the keymap does the following:\n\n1. Exit insert mode,\n\n2. Then use `vim.schedule` to \"do something\",\n\n3. Finally return to insert mode\n\nMultiple repeated presses will only produce one \"atom\",  as if ignoring subsequent typed keys.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`init.lua`\n\n```lua\nCmdAtoms = {}\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"CmdAtom\", {\n\tcallback = function(ev)\n\t\ttable.insert(CmdAtoms, ev.data)\n\tend,\n})\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"i\", \"<C-j>\", function()\n\tvim.api.nvim_feedkeys(vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(\"<esc>\", true, false, true), \"n\", false)\n\tvim.schedule(function()\n\t\tvim.api.nvim_feedkeys(\"i\", \"n\", false)\n\tend)\nend)\n```\n\n`nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n\n\nThen type:\n`i<C-j><C-j><C-j><Esc>`\n`:= CmdAtoms`\n\nonly one Atom:\n```lua\n{ {\n    changed = false,\n    cmd = \"i\",\n    count = 1,\n    keys = \"1i\\27\",\n    lhs = \"1i\\27\",\n    moved = false,\n    pos = { 1, 0 },\n    type = \"insert\",\n    undoseq = 0\n  } }\n```\nLimited cognition,I don't quite understand the mechanism.\nThis might not be a problem, please understand.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpect this mapping, based on the user type, should be an \"atom\"???\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1418+gf97bcbdf77\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArach\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbob",
