            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> 2\\. Then use `vim.schedule` to \"do something\",\n\n`vim.schedule` is \"async\", like scheduling something on your calendar. A scheduled task happens later, so Nvim does not know how to group it into the current CmdAtom (other input could be received while the scheduled task is pending...).\n\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41415 tracks a potential story where plugins have more control over how an atom is defined or \"declared\". \n\nAlthough `vim.schedule` is async, it might make sense for scheduled work to gain a task-id, so a plugin could tell Nvim to \"complete\" the current CmdAtom when the task-id completes.\n\nI will keep this issue open to track that but I'm not really sure if it is feasible.",
