            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The particular steps you reported, are an interesting case, because the \"delimiters\" of the insert-session (`i...<esc>`) are programmatic (non-user-input), but you *did* send actual user-input *during* the session. \n\nAnd it turns out there is already a global (`maptick`) which lets us detect detect this kind of thing. So `CmdAtom` can capture an insert-session if there was user-input during the session, even if its delimiters were not \"user input\".\n\nThe `vim.schedule` is a red herring in this case, since it only \"enters\" an insert-session.",
